From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/35] Never take focus: the window appears without activation

The viewer often runs on the desktop of a person using it for something
else. IbashoNoActivate (on at every launch, not saved; set up before the
splash screen) keeps the viewer from ever activating or raising its own
window: it appears without activation just behind the window in use (behind
everything if that's topmost or unknown), there's no splash screen and no
taskbar flashing, restore and resize don't activate, minimizing doesn't
activate the next window, bringToFront and focusClient do nothing, and a
maximized start fills the screen's work area instead of maximizing (which
always activates). The window renders as before; the person can still click
it or Alt+Tab to it. External browser launches ask for no activation too.
